{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|# Vivida retention and monetization plan\\n2|\\n3|Last updated: 26 August 2026\\n4|\\n5|This is the implementation order for improving activation, retention, and\\n6|customer spend. It combines the repository and live-product audit with\\n7|aggregate production baselines. The order is intentional: measure the full\\n8|value and payment loop first, create a repeat-use habit second, and expand paid\\n9|inventory only after those foundations are measurable.\\n10|\\n11|## Measured baseline\\n12|\\n13|- 981 registered users; 564 MAU, 202 WAU, and 21 DAU at extraction.\\n14|- DAU / MAU is 3.7%.\\n15|- 73.7% of the measured signup cohort completed a birth profile, while 31.8%\\n16|  returned during days 1–7.\\n17|- 48.2% of MAU were active on one day only; 8.2% were active on 8+ days.\\n18|- 15,044 free credits were issued in the trailing 30 days versus 3,331 spent,\\n19|  a 4.52× supply-to-spend ratio. Purchased issuance was 140 credits across\\n20|  four users; the active-wallet median was 20 credits.\\n21|- Tarot and natal PDF reports generated 79.5% of credit consumption.\\n22|- Two users have made lifetime credit purchases and one PRO subscription was\\n23|  active at extraction. Those counts can overlap and are not summed as unique\\n24|  payers.\\n25|- Early AI chart chat and tarot usage correlate with stronger later retention,\\n26|  but both samples are small and should guide experiments rather than forecasts.\\n27|\\n28|## Priority order\\n29|\\n30|| Priority                    | Initiative                                         | Why now                                                                                                                                                                              | Success signal                                                                                 |\\n31|| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n32|| P0 — shipped 2026-08-22     | Full value and paywall measurement                 | We can see some value actions, but not the complete exposure → selection → shortfall → checkout → unlock journey.                                                                    | Reliable value, paywall, D1/D7/D30, and payer-conversion baselines.                            |\\n33|| P0 — shipped                | Preserve calculator data through signup/onboarding | The public calculator already collects the exact birth inputs onboarding asks for again.                                                                                             | Higher calculator-to-profile completion and shorter onboarding time.                           |\\n34|| P0 — shipped 2026-08-22     | First onboarding “aha” result                      | New users now see their personalized Big Three immediately, then receive tracked, prefilled AI question recommendations.                                                             | Higher first-value completion, recommendation click-through, and D1 return.                    |\\n35|| P0 — shipped 2026-08-22     | Credits vs PRO comparison                          | Public natal promos, natal and first-free-tarot result states, and the Credits hub now explain one-time credits versus monthly unlimited PRO before a balance shortfall.             | Higher monetization-choice click-through and payer conversion before users reach zero credits. |\\n36|| P0 — implemented 2026-08-22 | Signup-credit cohort test                          | Future signups are assigned 50/50 to 20 credits immediately or 10 immediately plus 5 after a 24-hour return; legacy balances remain untouched.                                       | Variant-level D1/D7 retention, seven-day credit use, and 30-day payer conversion.              |\\n37|| P1 — shipped 2026-08-26     | Daily “Today” ritual                               | Daily reading, chosen focus, server-truth streak, and lifetime milestones now create a compact reason to return.                                                                     | Higher DAU/MAU, active days per MAU, and D7 retention.                                         |\\n38|| P1 — shipped 2026-08-26     | Contextual paywalls and credit-economy experiments | Shortfalls now name the deficit, compare credits with PRO, recommend the smallest sufficient pack, and return to content after verified checkout. Repeatable free earning is capped. | Higher paywall-to-checkout and 30-day payer conversion without lower retention.                |\\n39|| P1 — shipped 2026-09-05     | Reading history and journal                        | Tarot, forecasts, and AI insight do not accumulate into durable personal value.                                                     ...", "duration_ms": 56, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791096908960}
